  "scope": "One disposable kind v0.32.0 cluster on the lab runner's digest-pinned Kubernetes v1.36.1 node image, using the ready bundled kindnet daemonset. Three case-owned namespaces contain three source Pods and two HTTP marker Pods; IPv4 TCP/8080 probes compare no-policy baseline with ingress isolation, namespaceSelector+podSelector conjunction, and one explicit source-to-approved-Service flow. A DNS phase checks the owned Service through the in-cluster kube-dns Service and CoreDNS endpoints, with client egress restricted to CoreDNS UDP/TCP 53 before a separate TCP/8080 application allowance. No external targets, scans, production CNI, monitoring flows, IPv6, hostNetwork/node paths, or admission/generation automation is tested.",
